1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:20,519
The cathedral was underground because the man who built it had been
banned from building anything else above ground. That was what the
driver told us. I believed him as soon as I saw the elevator. It held
six cars, had a chandelier, and played organ music while lowering us
through the bones of Midnight City.

2
00:00:20,769 --> 00:00:37,993
Shawna sat beside me in a white dress with a slit that could have
started its own criminal organization. Tank leaned against the back of
the elevator with his arms folded while Rosa checked whether the
chandelier had real diamonds in it. "Leave it," he told her.

3
00:00:38,243 --> 00:01:02,162
"I'm looking." "You looking with your bag open." Mercedes and Porsche
had come in boxing jackets over their dresses. Mercedes's said TEAM
AIDEN. Porsche's said HE ALREADY WON. They had commissioned them that
morning from a tailor who apparently understood the speed of history.
When the elevator stopped, the noise hit us first. Men shouting. Money
changing hands.

4
00:01:02,412 --> 00:01:26,070
Music loud enough to move somebody's religion around. The cathedral's
old columns rose around a boxing ring built where an altar might once
have stood. Above it hung six giant screens. Below them, rows of
velvet seats held rich people who wanted to see poor decisions happen
close enough to feel expensive. At the far end of the ring stood the
champion.

5
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:50,304
Malik "Graveyard" Gault was thirty-three and looked like a building
that had learned resentment. He wore black gloves, black trunks, and a
chain thick enough to tow a boat. Somebody had tattooed a crown across
his chest. Underneath it were eleven little marks. Years undefeated.
Nigga, he was about to need a new tattoo arrangement. He watched me
cross the floor.

6
00:01:50,554 --> 00:02:14,088
"That the nigga?" His voice came through the speakers because somebody
had put a microphone too close to a man who should've been left to
breathe quietly. "That the college nigga?" I stopped beneath the ring
lights. "Valedictorian. Nigga, say it with the whole education." The
crowd laughed. Gault didn't. "And the cop nigga?" I touched the badge
on my jacket. "Captain.

7
00:02:14,338 --> 00:02:36,027
You checking the nigga's credentials before you lose?" "And this nigga
sings?" Shawna answered before I could. "When he feels like it.
Usually when the nigga hears a song he can improve." Gault leaned on
the ropes. "What this nigga when he bleeds?" "Still better dressed
than you," Rosa called. "You asked about four niggas and they all him.

8
00:02:36,277 --> 00:02:53,793
Which one you ready for?" Tank turned his head away so Gault wouldn't
see him laughing. It didn't work. Nigga, Tank's shoulders were shaking
like a truck at a red light. Vesper sat in a raised box beside an
empty chair draped in black cloth. Zero's chair.

9
00:02:54,043 --> 00:03:17,732
He wasn't there, but he had arranged for his absence to take up more
room than everybody else's body. Rusk stood beneath the box with a
scroll. "The captain enters three trials. Strength, courage,
dominion." "Y'all named three fights like they got degrees." "The
first is fought against the chosen hand of the cathedral. The second
against the reigning champion.

10
00:03:17,982 --> 00:03:42,644
The third is determined by the queen." "And if I win?" Vesper leaned
forward. "A seat among the criminal kings." "I sat in the throne
yesterday." "Yes. We noticed." A thin older man approached carrying my
gloves. He had silver hair cut close, a straight back, and a scar that
crossed one cheek without disturbing the calm around his eyes. His
suit was dark blue.

11
00:03:42,894 --> 00:04:03,653
Unlike everybody else in the room, he wasn't trying to look dangerous.
That made me watch him more carefully. "Bastien Moreau," he said. "I
will keep the rounds." "You a referee?" "Tonight." "What were you
yesterday?" "Tired." I liked the nigga immediately. He checked my
gloves while Shawna helped me take off my jacket.

12
00:04:03,903 --> 00:04:25,891
A few women near the ring started calling out before the shirt even
cleared my shoulders. "Wait till he breathes," Porsche told them. "You
haven't seen the shoulders move yet." Shawna looked around the crowd
with a little smile, then put her palm on my chest where everybody
could see whose hand belonged there. The shouting doubled. I bent and
kissed her.

13
00:04:26,141 --> 00:04:45,111
"How fast you want this done?" "Fast enough that my dinner's still
hot. Slow enough they learn your name." "Baby, that's a narrow
window." "You're gifted." My first opponent wore a red mask and had
two attendants carrying a hammer behind him. I looked at the hammer. I
looked at Bastien.

14
00:04:45,361 --> 00:05:08,438
"That's allowed?" "It is ceremonial." "Good, because my ceremony
didn't bring one." The red mask came over the ropes, bounced on his
feet, and hit his own chest three times. He was fast. I saw that
before he moved toward me. Some fighters advertise power because they
want you looking somewhere other than their feet. This one hardly
seemed to touch the floor.

15
00:05:08,688 --> 00:05:30,384
The bell rang. He threw three punches before I had finished deciding
where his face probably was under the mask. One caught my shoulder.
One brushed my ear. The third met my glove hard enough to wake my arm
all the way up. The crowd roared. "Aight," I said. "Nigga got
somewhere to be." He came again. I moved.

16
00:05:30,634 --> 00:05:52,684
His fist passed my face, and my short right turned the red mask far
enough that its left eyehole ended up beside his ear. The nigga threw
another punch at where I used to be. "Hold up." He froze with both
gloves raised. "That you talking?" "Nigga, who else you fighting?" He
tried to turn the mask with a glove and dragged it farther around.

17
00:05:52,934 --> 00:06:19,632
Bastien stepped between us. The whole cathedral booed. "Let him
fight!" somebody shouted. "Nigga can't see!" I shouted back. "Put a
bucket on your head and come demonstrate!" Porsche pointed into the
expensive seats. "That one. Purple suit. He volunteered." Purple Suit
immediately sat down. Bastien straightened the mask. My opponent
blinked through the proper holes and nodded once. The old man backed
away.

18
00:06:19,882 --> 00:06:42,088
The bell hadn't rung. The nigga knew it. He hit me in the ribs while I
was still looking at Purple Suit. "Oh, you ungrateful motherfucker."
"We fighting," he said. "Fair." He came after the laugh in my mouth.
Quick left, quicker right. I caught the right, stepped close, and put
a clean shot into his body. His breath went out. His knees followed.

19
00:06:42,338 --> 00:07:00,526
I backed off and let Bastien count. At eight he lifted a glove.
"Finished." I helped him up. "Name?" "Adrian." "Adrian, my nigga, you
got good feet. Let your eyes join the team next time." He pulled off
the mask and looked at it with personal disappointment.

20
00:07:00,776 --> 00:07:24,126
"My brother said that." "Your brother here?" A man three rows back
stood up so fast he hit the seat ahead of him. "I TOLD THAT NIGGA!"
Adrian shut his eyes. This, apparently, hurt worse than the body shot.
"Nigga, get him a microphone," Tank said. "Do not get that nigga a
microphone," Adrian said. The audience finally cheered the right man.

21
00:07:24,376 --> 00:07:46,249
Adrian smiled despite himself, then held the mask toward me. "Sign
it?" "After that sneaky rib punch?" "You said fair." "Nigga remembered
the ruling. What's your brother called?" "Luis." I borrowed a pen from
ringside and wrote inside the mask: LUIS WAS RIGHT. Then my name.
Adrian read it. His whole mouth fell open.

22
00:07:46,499 --> 00:08:09,819
"Nigga, I meant your signature." "That's beneath the medical advice."
He laughed. Luis came down the aisle demanding to inspect the
document, and Adrian went through the ropes holding it above his head
where his brother couldn't reach. "You were fast," I called after him.
"Come back with your face next time." He turned long enough to nod.
Heard that part. Kept it.

23
00:08:10,069 --> 00:08:26,112
Shawna pressed cold water into my hand when I reached our corner. "You
let him hit you." "Nigga took advantage of my community work." She
checked my ribs with two fingers. "Do your community work after the
bell." Tank leaned over her shoulder.

24
00:08:26,362 --> 00:08:50,931
"And quit signing evidence while there's two more niggas waiting to
produce some." "One." "You keeping count?" "I'm keeping dinner warm in
my imagination." Before Gault entered, a man in a silver jacket
climbed up beside our corner carrying a little board covered in
betting prices. "Captain, the odds have changed." "Nigga, I ain't
changed. Catch the board up." He swallowed.

25
00:08:51,181 --> 00:09:14,305
"You are still the underdog." Tank leaned over him. "That nigga what?"
"The underdog. In the market." "Nigga, look up. Does that look
underneath anything?" The man stared at my shoulders, then at the
people behind him calling my name, then at Shawna wiping my face as if
the whole room had been built to make sure she could reach me without
standing on tiptoe.

26
00:09:14,555 --> 00:09:38,909
"The champion has eleven years—" "Nigga, we heard the years," I said.
"We about to discuss the minutes." Mercedes came over with Porsche and
a stack of betting slips thick enough to make the man reconsider which
direction he wanted to leave. "We backed Aiden," Mercedes said.
"Obviously," Porsche added. The silver jacket looked alarmed. "How
much?" Porsche told him.

27
00:09:39,159 --> 00:10:02,255
Nigga, his face lost money just hearing it. "That is a significant
exposure." "Then cover your ass with a better opinion," she said. He
hurried away. Shawna looked at the slips. "You two bet that much?" "On
him?" Mercedes pointed at me like the answer should've been visible
from space. "Baby, this nigga lands cars where helicopters get
nervous.

28
00:10:02,505 --> 00:10:24,160
I know a sound investment when it takes its shirt off." Porsche handed
Shawna one slip. "That's yours." My wife looked at it, then at me.
"Now you really need to win." "Nigga, I was planning to lose
economically till you said that." She laughed and kissed my shoulder.
Tank leaned close while the women returned to their seats. "Listen.

29
00:10:24,410 --> 00:10:43,092
This nigga ain't one of those pretty fighters who gets surprised by a
punch. He good." "I know." "I seen him move." "So have I." "Then don't
be so busy being the greatest nigga in the building that you forget
this nigga brought both hands." I looked at my brother. He wasn't
doubting me.

30
00:10:43,342 --> 00:10:57,132
A nigga who loves you will sometimes be the only person in the room
willing to remind you that your blood still works like everybody
else's. I touched his fist with mine. "I got you." "You better have
you.

31
00:10:57,382 --> 00:11:20,676
I already got me." "Nigga, that's a beautiful sentence from a man who
lost his room key twice today." "The hotel got too many doors." We
laughed together, and the laugh loosened something under my ribs the
crowd couldn't reach. Then Gault entered without music. The cathedral
supplied its own. Eleven years made a heavy noise. Men stood when he
passed.

32
00:11:20,926 --> 00:11:41,547
Women touched the edge of his robe. His attendants put the chain
around a wooden stand shaped like a kneeling man. I looked at the
stand. "Nigga, your necklace got staff?" He hit me before the crowd
finished laughing. The punch landed on my gloves and still sent me
backward. My heels touched the ropes.

33
00:11:41,797 --> 00:12:03,131
Something sharp went through my ribs, a little hello from all the
trouble my body had survived before this city thought it was special.
Gault came after me. He was not slow. That was the dangerous part. Big
men sometimes give you enough time to admire how much they're bringing
toward you. This nigga brought it right now.

34
00:12:03,381 --> 00:12:26,854
I ducked one punch and took another against my side. The cathedral
tilted. I heard Tank shout, but the words were lost beneath the blood
rushing through my ears. Gault leaned close. "Stay down when I put you
there." "Nigga, you talking about next week? Do something." He did. He
caught me hard enough that one knee touched the canvas. The crowd
exploded.

35
00:12:27,104 --> 00:12:47,852
Shawna didn't move. Her eyes stayed on mine. There was no panic in
them, and somehow that hurt more than panic would've. She believed I
knew what I was doing. I had to become the man she was looking at
before the next bell. I stood. Gault smiled for the first time.
"Good." I wiped my mouth with the back of my glove.

36
00:12:48,102 --> 00:13:10,079
"Nigga, you enjoy that?" "Very much." "Remember it pretty. Tell your
niggas you had me kneeling." "I'll tell them I had you down." "Then
explain how this nigga got back up while you were practicing the
story." I changed the fight. Stopped giving him the straight line.
Made him turn. Let his shoulders tell me what his gloves were lying
about.

37
00:13:10,329 --> 00:13:29,938
When he swung at my head, I wasn't there. When he turned to find me, I
put a fist where his breath had been. The first good shot made his
smile disappear. The second made the crowd quiet. The third made Tank
climb halfway onto the ring apron before Rosa pulled him down by the
back of his jacket.

38
00:13:30,188 --> 00:13:54,111
"Nigga, let the man work!" "That's my nigga! I'm supporting!" "Then
support him from the floor. Nigga, you shaking his whole workplace!"
Gault drove me into the corner. I could feel blue thunder waiting
under my skin, eager and expensive. I left it there. Nigga, I wasn't
about to need lightning to convince this man my name was Aiden. He
swung wide.

39
00:13:54,361 --> 00:14:17,087
I stepped inside, hit him twice, and moved before the answer came. His
glove struck the corner post. The sound made everybody flinch except
him. Then he came at me angry. That was when he became easier. Not
easy. A storm ain't easy because you can see it. But anger told me
where his next foot would land before he knew himself.

40
00:14:17,337 --> 00:14:36,944
I gave him room he couldn't use and took back room he thought he
owned. By the next bell, he was breathing through his mouth. Bastien
came between us. "Corners." Gault didn't turn. He stared at me, chest
rising hard. "You really don't have to do this," he said quietly.
"Nigga, I'm in the ring.

41
00:14:37,194 --> 00:15:01,971
We past invitations." "If you win, he doubles what I owe." For the
first time, I looked beyond the fighter and saw the chain stand, the
attendants, the empty black chair. Eleven years undefeated. Eleven
years belonging to somebody. I went to my corner. Shawna put the towel
against my face. "What?" "Zero owns his debt." "Can you buy it?"
"Probably." "Then win first.

42
00:15:02,221 --> 00:15:22,883
Men like that hear money better when you're standing." She kissed the
clean side of my mouth. Nigga, how was I supposed to lose after that?
The last round started with Gault trying to take my whole head home. I
let him come. Took what I had to take. Gave more back. The ring shook
beneath us. The crowd stood.

43
00:15:23,133 --> 00:15:44,859
Somebody threw a glass and Bastien caught it against his jacket
without taking his eyes off the fight. Gault hit the ropes. I hit him
once more, clean and final, and the big man sat down like a building
had decided it needed a minute. He tried to stand at five. Tried again
at seven. At nine, I held out my hand.

44
00:15:45,109 --> 00:16:03,778
He looked at it. The bell rang. I kept the hand there. He took it.
Nigga, the sound that room made could have raised the cathedral to
street level. Shawna came through the ropes and nearly took me off my
feet herself. Tank shouted my name like he was mad at anybody who
hadn't heard it.

45
00:16:04,028 --> 00:16:28,008
Mercedes kissed Porsche on the cheek, then told her not to get ideas
because she'd just been overwhelmed by athletic excellence. Vesper
rose in her box. "The second trial is complete." I held Gault's wrist
up with mine. "The nigga's debt is complete too." She went still.
"That is not a prize you were offered." "Then offer it now." A murmur
passed through the kings.

46
00:16:28,258 --> 00:16:48,533
They didn't mind money changing hands. They minded somebody deciding
which hands mattered. Vesper looked toward the empty chair. "The
emperor will expect compensation." "Tell him send an invoice with a
picture of his face on it so I know who to disappoint." Gault let out
one shocked laugh. I looked at him.

47
00:16:48,783 --> 00:17:12,677
"Nigga, you free enough to laugh yet?" "I think so." "Then make it a
good one. That's your laugh now." He tried again. Louder. The nigga
looked surprised by how far his own voice could travel without waiting
for somebody to allow it. "That nigga laughing," Tank shouted. "I hear
him," Rosa said. "Nah. Nigga laughing like he got tomorrow." Gault
heard that too.

48
00:17:12,927 --> 00:17:36,884
He looked at my brother and nodded, once, hard. Vesper descended from
her box and approached the ring. Bastien held the ropes for her. She
didn't climb in. She stood outside with one hand resting on the top
rope, looking at me like the evening had stopped following the order
she'd memorized. "The final trial," she said, "is dominion. You may
claim the cathedral's purse.

49
00:17:37,134 --> 00:17:59,478
Ten million. Or you may purchase the champion's freedom." The room
quieted again. Gault's hand fell from mine. "Take the purse," he said.
"Nigga, be quiet." "I mean it." "I know. That's why I told you to be
quiet." I looked at Vesper. "Buy his freedom." She studied me for a
long second. "Done." The cheering started, but I lifted my glove.

50
00:17:59,728 --> 00:18:23,407
"And I'm charging the cathedral eleven million for the fight." Shawna
bent forward laughing. Rusk actually grabbed the rail. "You cannot
simply—" "Nigga, I just sold out your dead church, beat your champion,
saved your parade yesterday, and brought my own beautiful wife. You
think all that come free?" Vesper put her hand over her mouth. It
didn't hide the smile.

51
00:18:23,657 --> 00:18:45,944
The old silver-bearded king from dinner stood in the front row. "I'll
pay it." Everybody turned. His wife pulled him back down by his
sleeve. "We'll pay it," she corrected. That was how I won three
trials, freed a champion, and left a million ahead of where the queen
had meant to put me. Gault met us outside the changing room afterward.

52
00:18:46,194 --> 00:19:08,266
Without the chain, he looked younger. Not smaller. Just less arranged
for somebody else's benefit. "If you need me," he said, "send word."
"I need you to go eat something you chose yourself." He nodded, then
looked at Shawna. "Your husband is—" "I know," she said. Gault smiled.
"No. Nigga, I don't think anybody knows all of it yet.

53
00:19:08,516 --> 00:19:29,944
I came in here thinking I knew the man I'd have to fight." "And?" she
asked. "The nigga I needed to meet showed up afterward. Same face.
Same hands. Different damn use for them." She looked at me, proud
enough to make my battered ribs sit up straighter. Nigga, I liked him
better every minute. Bastien waited by the elevator.

54
00:19:30,194 --> 00:19:50,478
While everybody else celebrated, he slipped a folded card into my
hand. No crown on it. No fancy threat. Just an address and a time.
"There is a woman who ought to have seen that fight," he said. "Who?"
He looked toward Vesper, standing alone beneath the cathedral's last
chandelier.

55
00:19:50,728 --> 00:20:14,094
"Someone she was before this city taught her what love cost." Before I
could ask another question, the elevator doors opened. Shawna took my
arm. The whole room applauded as we went up. I looked at the card
again once the city lights returned. A garden. Tomorrow afternoon.
Underneath the address, in a different hand, somebody had written:
COME WITHOUT A CROWN.

56
00:20:14,344 --> 00:20:36,287
"You going?" Shawna asked. I folded it and put it beside my badge.
"Depends if they got dinner." "Baby." "Nigga freed a champion. Let him
investigate a menu." "You already decided." I smiled at her. "Yeah. We
going. But your nigga taking snacks. I can't keep changing these
people's lives on ceremonial portions."
